FerrionOS change to Zed (gpui, gpui_linux, gpui_platform and util: Apache-2.0; the other crates: GPL-3.0-or-later; licenses kept), made against release v1.29.3, commit d01b134cddf5e4f71964deb2d6f81cdb38fcf1e7:
- gpui_linux builds for x86_64-unknown-redox, and gpui_platform uses it; gpui exposes the items gpui_linux needs there. Without the wayland or x11 feature it runs headless. Its realtime thread keeps the default priority, as the libc crate has no SCHED_FIFO for this target.
- gpui: the screen-capture frame type is empty on this target.
- util: increase_open_file_limit does nothing, as nix has no sys::resource for this target.
- cli: built as on Linux; ipc-channel uses its in-process backend, so cli cannot yet hand paths to a running editor.
- fs: directories are read with std::fs::read_dir (rustix has no Dir for this target), and FileHandle::current_path reports that it is unsupported.
- client: telemetry names the OS FerrionOS and reads its version from /etc/os-release.
- settings: the VS Code import reads the Linux terminal keys.
- languages: rust-analyzer, ty, ruff and pyrefly have no release asset for this target, so they must be on PATH.

